search index=threatmap sourcetype="zabbix:problems"
``` Template: Zabbix problems (real-time export or webhook, JSON). ```
``` Modele : problemes Zabbix (export temps reel ou webhook, JSON).
    A ADAPTER : index, sourcetype, id du site. Champs lus, ceux de l'export temps reel
    de Zabbix : eventid, value (1 = probleme, 0 = retour a la normale), name,
    severity (0 a 5), clock, hosts[].
    Ce ne sont pas des attaques : pas d'origine, donc pas d'arc sur la carte. Ajoutez
    "Interne" a origins.masked_labels dans la configuration. ```
| spath
``` Splunk extrait deja les champs d'un evenement JSON recu par le HEC : spath les double.
    On retire les doublons. ```
| foreach * [ eval "<<FIELD>>" = mvdedup('<<FIELD>>') ]
| where tonumber(value) == 1
| dedup eventid
| eval _time = coalesce(tonumber(clock), _time),
       niveau = tonumber(severity),
       signature = name,
       dest_host = coalesce(mvindex('hosts{}.name', 0), mvindex('hosts{}.host', 0))
| eval severity = case(niveau == 5, "critical", niveau == 4, "high", niveau == 3, "medium",
                       niveau == 2, "low", true(), "informational")
| eval src_ip = "0.0.0.0", Country = "Interne", src_lat = "", src_lon = "",
       action = "alerted",
       dc = "DC-NORD"
| fields _time, src_ip, Country, src_lat, src_lon, dc, severity, signature, dest_host, action
